# __TITLE__

__DESCRIPTION__

Built with [s:CMS](https://github.com/lad-sapienza/scms-core), on top of [Astro](https://astro.build).

## Commands

| Command | Action |
|---|---|
| `npm install` | Install dependencies |
| `npm run dev` | Start the local dev server at `localhost:4321` |
| `npm run build` | Build the production site to `./dist/` |
| `npm run preview` | Preview the production build locally |
| `npm run add-collection` | Scaffold a new content collection |
| `npm run add-content` | Add a new content file to an existing collection |
| `npm run images` | Convert content images to WebP (max 2000 px) and rewrite their references |

## Optimizing images

Drop JPG/PNG images next to your content as usual, then run `npm run images`: they are converted to WebP, scaled down to 2000 px, the originals are deleted and the `.md`/`.mdx` references are rewritten (`--dry-run` shows the savings without touching anything). References from `.astro`/`.tsx` files are only reported — update them by hand.

To make the build fail when an unoptimized image slips in, add a check to `package.json`; it never modifies any file:

```json
"prebuild": "scms-optimize-images --check"
```

Limits, quality and the site languages are configured in `src/user.config.mjs` (`userConfig.images`, `userConfig.i18n`); see the [scms-core README](https://github.com/lad-sapienza/scms-core#image-optimization) for all the options, including an optional pre-commit hook. Commit the `.scms-optimize-images.json` file it may create.

## Updating the framework

```bash
npm update @lad-sapienza/scms-core
```

## Dependabot

`.github/dependabot.yml` opens weekly pull requests for npm dependencies (s:CMS core on its own, minor and patch grouped, majors one by one; TypeScript majors are skipped because `@astrojs/check` does not support them yet) and monthly ones for GitHub Actions. Every pull request runs the build without deploying.

Patch-only pull requests are merged automatically by `.github/workflows/dependabot-automerge.yml`. For this to work, in the repository settings:

1. Enable **Allow auto-merge** (Settings → General).
2. Add a branch protection rule on `main` that requires the `build` status check and **Require branches to be up to date before merging**. Without it, a patch merged right after another can leave `package-lock.json` out of sync and break `npm ci`.

The workflows assume the default branch is called `main`; adjust the `branches` lists if yours is not.

## Project structure

```
src/
  content.config.ts     # Content collection schemas
  user.config.mjs        # Site configuration and metadata
  pages/                  # Routes
  layouts/                 # Layouts
  styles/global.css         # Stylesheet
public/                   # Static assets, served as-is
astro.config.mjs          # Registers the scms() integration
```

See the [s:CMS documentation](https://github.com/lad-sapienza/sCMS) for available components (`DataTb`, `Map`, `Gallery`, `ZoteroGeoViewer`, `Record`, and more).
